{
  "source_head": "109aab5063dc056f794ef2c98f8ba2d6ca0717a9",
  "scope": "Partial semantic review of thirty-two component and deployment/acceptance guides at source 109aab5; not exhaustive source validation or independent deployment",
  "all_documents_reviewed": false,
  "actual_public_renewal_accepted": false,
  "findings": [
    "Admission, durable CSR, role, CA account, private snapshots, HTTP-01 and finalization responsibilities remain separate.",
    "CA protocol fixtures, logically aged renewal, real native application and real public renewal-clock proof remain distinct.",
    "Explicit consent, original candidate/account identity, no raw secret logging, retained ambiguous outcomes and fail-closed boundary statements remain stated.",
    "Relay authority preparation/custody assertions, publication barriers, retained-operation recovery, served-TLS verification and offline quarantine remain separate; no automatic offline bypass is documented.",
    "Protected issuer host documentation separately states privileged host trust, narrow SQL identities, cleanup gates, original job/order/CSR retention and the actual fixture limitations. The public policy example still has the documented nine fields.",
    "Quickstart omitted the explicit --network-subnet argument despite asking the operator to select a subnet. Both init examples now pass the selected value; doctor examples are unchanged. This correction is a documentation follow-up, not a mutation of the frozen candidate.",
    "Certificate automation overview ended with a stale blanket protected-host-restoration gap. The follow-up now links merged isolated recovery while retaining public operator, real renewal-clock and durable encrypted off-host custody requirements. Original staged preparation/recovery failures remain historical failures."
  ],
